[4.283, "o", "\u001b[1;39m{\r\n  \u001b[0m\u001b[1;34m\"answer\"\u001b[0m\u001b[1;39m: \u001b[0m\u001b[0;32m\"Password spraying is a sub-technique of brute force (T1110.003) where the attacker tries one or a few very common passwords against many different accounts. It avoids account lockout because each account only sees one or two failures, which stays under typical lockout thresholds.\"\u001b[0m\u001b[1;39m,\r\n  \u001b[0m\u001b[1;34m\"sources\"\u001b[0m\u001b[1;39m: \u001b[0m\u001b[1;39m[\r\n    \u001b[0;39m3\u001b[0m\u001b[1;39m\r\n  \u001b[1;39m]\u001b[0m\u001b[1;39m,\r\n  \u001b[0m\u001b[1;34m\"confident\"\u001b[0m\u001b[1;39m: \u001b[0m\u001b[0;39mtrue\u001b[0m\u001b[1;39m\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[1;39m}\u001b[0m\r\n"]
